usage: branchwrite [-h]
                   {check,canonicalize,run,step,doctor,prepare-base,context-status,code,resume,apply,export,review,status,reconcile} ...

Inspect .bw syntax or execute a host-authorized workflow.

positional arguments:
  {check,canonicalize,run,step,doctor,prepare-base,context-status,code,resume,apply,export,review,status,reconcile}
    doctor              Check real client file and shell isolation without
                        inference.
    prepare-base        Build context from project files and saved COW
                        branches, or admit an existing verified pack.
    context-status      Show the last durable project-context step and COW
                        receipts without inference.
    code                Start coding in an owned copy with explicit file
                        grants.
    resume              Resume a saved coding setup without changing its task
                        or source.
    apply               Apply a pinned export into a new owned project copy.
    export              Export complete reviewed changes into a new archive.
    review              Inspect recorded file-tool changes without
                        publication.
    status              Read recorded run status without execution or
                        inference.
    reconcile           Recover proven durable output for one pending model
                        operation; does not advance the workflow.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
